From: Cristian Papa <pcristian292@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 20:30:00 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] net: airoha: xpon: keep 512 black box events per bank

The sampler alone adds six events per second and every downstream PLOAM
adds three, so 256 events may cover only a few tens of seconds. The OLT
deactivations seen on the lab line follow up to ten seconds of errors and
the interesting history can be longer. Keep 512 events per bank (32 KiB for
both banks) and allocate the per-open debugfs copy with kvzalloc(), as it
grows to about 16 KiB.

Signed-off-by: Cristian Papa <pcristian292@gmail.com>
---
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_xpon_blackbox.h	2026-10-19 20:24:23.215738177 -0300
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_xpon_blackbox.h	2026-10-19 20:24:23.227738175 -0300
@@ -8,7 +8,7 @@
 #include <linux/slab.h>
 #include <linux/seq_file.h>
 
-#define GPON_BB_SIZE 256
+#define GPON_BB_SIZE 512
 #define GPON_BB_PRINT 24
 #define GPON_BB_UNKNOWN U32_MAX
 
@@ -430,14 +430,14 @@
 	int ret;
 
 	/* debugfs protects this open operation against removal. */
-	snap = kzalloc(sizeof(*snap), GFP_KERNEL);
+	snap = kvzalloc(sizeof(*snap), GFP_KERNEL);
 	if (!snap)
 		return -ENOMEM;
 	ret = gpon_bb_copy_snapshot(bb, snap, last);
 	if (!ret)
 		ret = single_open(file, gpon_bb_show, snap);
 	if (ret)
-		kfree(snap);
+		kvfree(snap);
 	return ret;
 }
 
@@ -455,7 +455,7 @@
 {
 	struct seq_file *s = file->private_data;
 
-	kfree(s->private);
+	kvfree(s->private);
 	return single_release(inode, file);
 }
 
